course: dictionary
lesson: 4868
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Icing can mean a sweet topping for cakes, but it can also mean ice forming on something. The words around it tell you which meaning is right. In «paska is a tall Easter bread with white icing», the bread and the sweet white covering show that icing is food here.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide. In «the burnt edge was cut out of the picture, and a filter made the icing shine», the picture and the filter tell you that icing is the sugary topping on a cake. Ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some words belong to phrases, and the whole phrase has its own meaning. «The icing on the cake» means something extra that makes a good thing even better. You do not need to eat a cake to understand it. Look at the whole phrase, not just one word at a time.
fact: Icing is a sweet topping made of sugar, often with butter or water, that covers cakes and biscuits.
fact: In the USA, icing is often called frosting.
fact: Icing can also mean ice forming on something, like the wings of a plane. Icing on roads and planes is dangerous.
fact: «The icing on the cake» means something extra that makes a good thing even better.
fact: Ice, ices, iced and icing are forms of the same verb, so the past tense of ice is iced.
exercise: «Paska is a tall Easter bread with white icing.» In this sentence, what is icing? | Ice forming on the wings of a plane | *A sweet topping made of sugar | A kind of Easter festival | A tall, thin loaf
exercise: The pilot warned that icing on the wings was dangerous. What is icing in this sentence? | Sugar sprinkled on bread | A sweet topping on a cake | A type of biscuit | *Ice forming on something
exercise: «The icing on the cake» means what? | *Something extra that makes a good thing even better | Frosting that is too thin | A plate for serving cakes | A cake that has gone bad
test: In the USA, what is icing often called? | Crumble | Sponge | Batter | *Frosting
test: Yesterday she ___ the cupcakes with pink sugar. Which word fits? | icing | *iced | ices | ice
exam: Mum said, «Don't put icing on the cake until it has cooled.» Which meaning of icing is used here? | *A sweet topping | A kind of cake tin | Ice forming on something | Something extra that makes things better
